# The chronicler writes a closed visit up, and the journal keeps the paragraph and the milestones.
#
# Under --playground no request is made: the chronicler writes a fixed placeholder the moment a group
# is queued, which is what lets a script follow the queue and the save. The foreground/background
# gate and the preemption need a real model and are measured by hand (design/BELLIC_JOURNAL_REPORT.md).
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Hall" --period noon --observe-only "brewer"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
advance 12 180
expect-state journal kind=Narration state=Raw

# Leaving closes the visit; the chronicler takes it up on the next frame.
click button
wait mode WorldView 60
wait 1
expect-state journal pending-groups=0
expect-state journal written-groups=1
expect-state journal kind=Milestone
expect-no-state journal kind=Narration state=Pending

manage Journal
wait 1
expect [chronicle]
expect First came to the
expect-not not yet written up
save roundtrip
quit
